      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Pub/Sub Provider**\n\nI've decided to use Google Cloud Pub/Sub as the external provider. This should be a straightforward implementation, and the first step is to get the Google Cloud Pub/Sub client library in place.\n\n\n**Defining the Consume Function**\n\nI'm now focused on the `consume_event.py` file. I'm writing the function to consume a single message, and I'm importing the `pubsub_v1` library from `google.cloud`. I'm constructing the subscription path using the project and subscription IDs, and will use a `SubscriberClient` to pull the message. Time to get this code working!\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789861767225,
          "start": 1789861765031
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc131fa7001D00hYkhmRW6NsF",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc131bfa001JfDxo25KatSNR7",
      "session_id": "ses_f43ece417ffeY6Xs0cUWekAAz4",
      "time_created": 1789861765031,
      "time_updated": 1789861767226
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "ODqjwXr9xoPm3Zt4",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "from google.cloud import pubsub_v1\nimport os\n\ndef consume_one_message(project_id: str, subscription_id: str):\n    \"\"\"Consumes one message from a Pub/Sub subscription.\"\"\"\n    \n    subscriber = pubsub_v1.SubscriberClient()\n    subscription_path = subscriber.subscription_path(project_id, subscription_id)\n\n    response = subscriber.pull(\n        request={\"subscription\": subscription_path, \"max_messages\": 1},\n        timeout=30.0,\n    )\n\n    if response.received_messages:\n        for received_message in response.received_messages:\n            print(f\"Received message: {received_message.message.data.decode('utf-8')}\")\n            subscriber.acknowledge(\n                request={\"subscription\": subscription_path, \"ack_ids\": [received_message.ack_id]}\n            )\n            print(f\"Acknowledged message: {received_message.ack_id}\")\n            return received_message.message.data.decode('utf-8')\n    else:\n        print(\"No messages received.\")\n        return None\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Replace with your Google Cloud Project ID and Subscription ID\n    project_id = os.environ.get(\"GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT_ID\")\n    subscription_id = os.environ.get(\"GOOGLE_CLOUD_SUBSCRIPTION_ID\")\n\n    if not project_id or not subscription_id:\n        print(\"Please set the GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT_ID and GOOGLE_CLOUD_SUBSCRIPTION_ID environment variables.\")\n    else:\n        consume_one_message(project_id, subscription_id)\n",
            "filePath": "consume_event.py"
          },
